+ * including the DOMINANT self-munmap vae1 (live-captured asid=1 va=0x117ce000 this session). */
+static inline void aios_asid_gen_invalidate(asid_t asid)
+{
+#ifdef ENABLE_SMP_SUPPORT
+    /* CORESCHED S2: if this asid is resident on a PEER core, that peer is actively running the
+     * vspace under its (shared) hw asid -- ABANDONING the hw (clear) would let the value be
+     * reissued to another vspace while the peer still uses it = a silent cross-process stale hit.
+     * So instead do the residency-masked `tlbi` for the hw asid on all resident cores (self's
+     * local tlbi + the masked remote IPI) and KEEP the binding, so self + peers stay coherent
+     * under the shared hw asid. This is the ORIGINAL residency-shootdown path, used ONLY for a
+     * genuinely peer-resident vspace -- i.e. only under coresched, where the fabric is WARM
+     * (active multi-core), so the tlbi does NOT hit the after-idle stall. DORMANT under the
+     * default all-threads-on-core-0 config: aios_asid_residency is always {core0} there, so the
+     * peer test is false and we fall through to the no-tlbi abandon path (the stall cure). */
+    word_t resid = aios_asid_residency(asid);
